# SAMPLE picks among bank 1's three samples (the third has a LIST chunk
# before its data -- the 44-byte-header trap); BANK (Shift, P3) moves to bank 2.
# Free-running adopts each break's tempo, so J7's eighths prove which loaded:
# 120 BPM = 8 per 2 s, 170 BPM = ~11, 100 BPM = ~7.
pot 1 0
pot 2 0
pot 3 0
pot 4 0.5
pot 6 0.5
wait 3000
expect led b1 green
pot 3 0.5                  # sample 2: 170 BPM mono, 32 slices
wait 1500
expect led b1 green
mark
wait 2000
expect rms > 0.01
expect edges 7 > 10        # 170 BPM
pot 3 0.95                 # sample 3: the LIST-chunk WAV, 120 BPM
wait 1500
expect led b1 green
mark
wait 2000
expect rms > 0.01
expect edges 7 < 10        # back to 120
expect edges 7 > 6
press b3                   # Shift page
wait 100
pot 3 0                    # sweep through the stored BANK so the pot catches
wait 200
pot 3 0.99                 # BANK -> bank 2 (100 BPM)
wait 300
release b3
wait 1500
expect led b1 green
mark
wait 2000
expect rms > 0.01
expect edges 7 < 8
expect finite
